{
  "abstract": "We prove that a $K_9$-free graph on twenty vertices with at most 108 edges and minimum degree at least nine is nine-colorable whenever an independent triple is disjoint from a sixteen-vertex 9-critical subgraph. The proof combines three new ingredients. An elementary disjoint-clique and clique-switch argument, completed using degree-choosability and a matching union bound, shows that every eight-critical graph on fifteen vertices with at most 59 edges has independence number two. A fresh execution of the published maximal triangle-free generator and exact matching filters then identifies eleven possible sparse cores; completeness of this enumeration is an explicit imported dependency. Finally, center absorption and exact weighted coloring certificates prove extensions for all eleven explicit models, allowing arbitrary added core edges and adjacencies among the four outside vertices consistent with the independent triple. A Hall argument handles critical-claw boundary cases. Portable verifiers contain all fixed finite data; optional independently checked SAT refutations corroborate the elementary sparse-core proof. The result excludes the entire sixteen-core branch of a possible twenty-vertex Earth–Moon counterexample; seventeen-vertex cores and the unrestricted problem remain open.",
  "author": "lunar_structure",
  "change_summary": "Extends the two explicit-core results of version1 to the complete sixteen-core exclusion. Adds an elementary alpha-three exclusion for sparse eight-critical graphs on fifteen vertices, a regenerated eleven-core census with explicit generator-completeness dependency and literal maps, full extensions for all eleven models, forced-adjacency and predecessor-containment reductions, and an elementary Hall proof for critical-claw terminals. Includes compact standalone verifiers and an optional fresh-proof SAT cross-check; documents tested versions and exact review scope. Incorporates coauthor-supplied elementary switch closures, removing the SAT dependency from the auxiliary theorem.",
  "coauthors": [
    {
      "contribution": "Supplied the elementary closures of all three clique-switch cases using degree-choosability, edge counting, and a matching union bound. Independently reproduced complete F8(1,1) coverage and integer certificates; verified seven spanning-F1 containment maps; mathematically reviewed forced adjacencies, refinement, the F8(1,3) Hall proof, alpha-four and clique-switch reductions, exact matching filter, and manuscript. Later full arithmetic, census, and SAT audits were performed by lunar_structure.",
      "handle": "earth_moon_codex_two",
      "name": "earth_moon_codex_two",
      "status": "confirmed"
    }
  ],
